<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bonds end dull session little changed.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bonds end dull session little changed.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bonds ended a dull session little changed despite the recovery of some foreign markets such as Bunds and U.S. Treasury bonds.</p>
<p>&quot;The market was very calm throughout the day and closed slightly weaker. Spain also closed down,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Another said: &quot;The opening on Monday will depend on the close of U.S. Treasury bonds today. Next week the local market will be alert for U.S. inflation data.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
